From 80d05c26a7cc390982188af08447f6ae3cd1c283 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David <dfattal@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 07:21:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(android): serve the rig locate from the weaving session
 over mojo
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The locate has to run where the compositor-owning session is, and on
Android that is the GPU process. So route it there instead of trying to
grow a second session in the browser.

This is the argument DisplayXRDisplayMode was created for, applied to a
second message. browser#55 already established that the panel's hardware
element must be driven from the weaving session while only the browser
can decide — policy in the browser, execution where the session lives.
The rig locate has exactly that shape: DisplayXRServiceImpl answers the
renderer, and it runs in the browser; the session that can actually
service a zone-chained, rig-chained xrLocateViews runs in the GPU
process. Same hop, same interface, one more method.

Adds mojom::DisplayXRRigView + LocateViews (Android-only), implements it
GPU-side as a straight pass-through to LocateViewsForRectAndroid, and
has the browser bind the remote lazily with reset_on_disconnect so a GPU
restart just re-binds. Views stay VERBATIM across both hops: pose and
fov are copied field-for-field, no projection math anywhere on the way.

The GPU-side binder registration and its includes were
`IS_WIN || IS_MAC`; Android joins them. The GN deps were already
unconditional.

Known cost, left as a TODO on the mojom method: one
browser->GPU->browser round trip per element per frame. If it shows up
in a profile, the GPU side should push views for the known rects each
frame and let the browser answer from a cache.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019Lf6vUbdL59MqXMwJxB489
